## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design incremental geometry data structures, reason about dominance, and assess batch-update trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Pareto frontier maintenance
- Batch incremental updates
- Monotone frontier properties (x increasing, y decreasing)
- Trade-offs: update time vs rebuild cost

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch: merge batch into frontier
function insertBatch(frontier, batch){
  batch.sort((a,b)=> a.x-b.x);
  // prune intra-batch dominated
  let filtered=[]; let maxY=-Infinity;
  for(let p of batch){ if(p.y>maxY){ filtered.push(p); maxY=p.y; } }
  // merge with frontier (frontier: sorted by x, y strictly decreasing)
  let i=0,j=0; let newFrontier=[];
  while(i<frontier.length || j<filtered.length){
    let a = frontier[i], b = filtered[j];
    if(!a) { newFrontier.push(...filtered.slice(j)); break; }
    if(!b) { newFrontier.push(...frontier.slice(i)); break; }
    if(a.x < b.x){ newFrontier.push(a); i++; }
    else if(b.x < a.x){ newFrontier.push(b); j++; }
    else { // equal x, keep larger y
      if(a.y > b.y){ newFrontier.push(a); i++; j++; }
      else { newFrontier.push(b); i++; j++; }
    }
  }
  // optional prune to maintain y-decreasing property
  return pruneFrontier(newFrontier);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world streaming analytics: maintaining a dynamic feature (distinct count) under batched updates with tight per-batch guarantees. It probes data structures (circular buffers, counters), amortized reasoning, and practical optimizations under constrained space. 

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window maintenance
- Distinct counting with frequency map
- Amortized analysis under batched updates
- Space-conscious data structures and optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton demonstrating the core idea
class WindowDistinct {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buf = new Array(W);
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.head = 0; // points to oldest element
    this.size = 0;
    this.distinct = 0;
  }
  init(arr) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.W; i++) this.push(arr[i]);
  }
  push(x) {
    if (this.size < this.W) this.size++;
    else {
      this.pop();
    }
    this.buf[this.head] = x;
    this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
    const c = (this.freq.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.freq.set(x, c);
    if (c === 1) this.distinct++;
  }
  pop() {
    const idx = (this.head) % this.W;
    const y = this.buf[idx];
    const c = this.freq.get(y) - 1;
    if (c === 0) this.freq.delete(y);
    else this.freq.set(y, c);
    if (c === 0) this.distinct--;
  }
  batchUpdate(batch) {
    for (const x of batch) this.push(x);
  }
  query() {
    return this.distinct;
  }
}
```

